      c("Why deficiency causes the symptoms", '<p>Less insulin → <strong>less muscle/adipose glucose uptake + more liver glucose production</strong> → hyperglycemia.</p><p>Hyperglycemia → <strong>osmotic diuresis → dehydration</strong>. More lipolysis/ketogenesis → DKA risk. More protein breakdown → weight loss/muscle wasting.</p><p>Learn these causal links; detailed DKA management belongs in the emergencies lecture.</p>', ["glucose-uptake-production", "osmotic-diuresis", "lipolysis-ketogenesis", "protein-weight-loss"], [q("Which chain explains dehydration in untreated insulin deficiency?", "Hyperglycemia → osmotic diuresis → fluid loss", ["Insulin excess → glucose storage → fluid retention", "Reduced liver glucose production → increased blood volume", "Protein breakdown alone → reduced urine output"], "Osmotic diuresis connects hyperglycemia to polyuria/dehydration."), q("Why does absolute insulin deficiency increase DKA risk?", "Increased lipolysis and ketogenesis", ["Complete suppression of fat breakdown", "Increased insulin-mediated storage", "Reduced hepatic glucose production"], "Lack of insulin promotes fat mobilization and ketone formation.")], [q("A patient with new T1DM loses weight despite eating more and has frequent urination. Which paired mechanisms explain this?", "Protein/fuel breakdown and hyperglycemia-driven osmotic diuresis", ["Increased glycogen storage and water retention", "Insulin excess and reduced liver glucose production", "Normal glucose uptake and reduced urinary losses"], "Insulin deficiency causes catabolism; hyperglycemia causes osmotic diuresis.")])
