      c("Pediatric goals balance benefit and safety", '<p>The lecture gives a pediatric goal around <strong>7%</strong> and emphasizes individualization.</p><p><strong>ADA clarification:</strong> &lt;7% is appropriate for most children/adolescents; selected patients can safely aim lower. Less stringent goals may fit hypoglycemia unawareness, inability to communicate lows, limited monitoring/technology access, or excessive treatment burden.</p><p><a href="https://doi.org/10.2337/dc26-s014" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ADA pediatric guidance</a>.</p>', ["pediatric-target", "pediatric-individualization"], [q("What principle governs a pediatric T1DM A1C target?", "A usual target below 7%, individualized for safety, monitoring access, and burden", ["Exactly 7% must be imposed regardless of severe lows", "Every child must achieve below 5%", "A1C targets never change with circumstances"], "The lecture’s approximate 7% goal is individualized; ADA specifies <7% for most.")], [q("A young child cannot reliably describe hypoglycemia and has recurrent severe lows. Should the team insist on the tightest possible A1C?", "No; individualize and consider a less stringent goal for safety", ["Yes; ignore low-glucose risk", "Yes; target selection is independent of monitoring ability", "No; stop all insulin replacement"], "The goal balances benefit with hypoglycemia risk; insulin remains necessary.")]),
      c("Adult goals balance long-term protection and hypoglycemia", '<p>The lecture’s usual adult A1C target is <strong>&lt;7%</strong>, balancing long-term microvascular/cardiovascular protection with hypoglycemia risk.</p><p>More or less stringent targets depend on the individual’s circumstances. A goal is not successful if achieving it repeatedly causes harmful lows.</p>', ["adult-target", "adult-benefit-risk"], [q("What usual adult A1C goal is given in the lecture?", "Below 7%, with individualization", ["Below 5% for every adult", "Exactly 9% for every adult", "No adult has an A1C goal"], "<7% is the lecture’s usual adult target; safety and circumstances matter.")], [q("An adult with T1DM achieves a very low A1C but has recurrent severe hypoglycemia. What should guide the next goal discussion?", "Rebalance glycemic benefit against hypoglycemia risk", ["Treat the lowest A1C as success regardless of harm", "Use the same target for every adult", "Classify the patient as T2DM because lows occur"], "Targets are individualized to avoid harm while supporting long-term benefit.")])
